  "findings": [
    "The corrected library fails the same original input on both a fresh database and the preserved prefix-7 seed. Inherited backlog or legacy segments cannot be the sole cause of failure in these Debug diagnostics.",
    "Ledger reconstruction is small in both runs. No copied-ledger fallback was used. This fixture does not support treating allocator copying as the remaining root-cause fix.",
    "Fresh-run replay publication overhead is approximately 109 seconds within approximately 120 seconds of replay wall time; completed full-text profiles report approximately 2.9 seconds of preparation. These counters overlap and exclude failed-operation profiles; they are not additive wall-time attribution.",
    "Mixed-index/enrichment eligibility restrictions and repeated runtime/source reconstruction remain relevant. Do not remove safety fences merely to admit those actors into the existing text-only cache.",
    "Retained journal records contain up to 1024 document keys and projected payloads in several consumer lanes. Bounded service throughput, whole-record quota recovery, and the duplicated lane payload representation warrant separate causal probes."
